+# ZEELICH-29 (#29, OPEN-TASKS.he.md: "Zeelich looks simpler than the Citadel")
+
+Evidence: **automated runtime only (SwiftShader, headless Chromium)**. Nobody played it. Nothing was checked on a real
+GPU, so there are no GPU, frame-time or load-time numbers.
+
+**The user picked it on 27.11 (relayed by the coordinator): it is the default now, with a second pass on top (§7).**
+`?zeelich29=old` gives the street as it was. With `old`:
+- `buildZeelich29` is never called;
+- `z29Clear` answers false;
+- the paving, kerb and granite textures and the lamps are the originals.
+
+The island is then exactly as before. §1–§4 describe the first pass, when it was still the candidate
+`?zeelich29=new`. The "before" numbers (`b2`) were taken on the committed tree with the switch off; they are the
+original street.
+
+## 1. What the Citadel has that Zeelich lacks (measured)
+**Method.**
+- The play camera (Follow, Far), Medium, 1366×768, chapter 3 on Zeelich.
+- Five Zeelich spots: the dock, the gate, the plaza, the main street east of the plaza, the council house.
+- Two Citadel spots: the square, Bug Street from the square.
+- Probe: `captures/zeelich-29/z29shots.mjs`.
+- Pixel measure: `detail.py`. "Fine detail" is the mean |L − its 9×9 mean|; "edges" is the share of pixels with a Sobel
+  edge over 24 levels. Both are measured below the sky band, without the HUD strip.
+
+| | fine detail | edges | furniture /100 m² | people /100 m² |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| Citadel square | 14.6 | 32 % | 5.75 | 2.43 |
+| Citadel, Bug Street | 13.2 | 28 % | 2.65 | 0.22 |
+| Zeelich dock | 7.2 | 12 % | 7.52 | 0.44 |
+| Zeelich gate | 7.6 | 14 % | 7.52 | 0.44 |
+| Zeelich plaza | 8.3 | 15 % | 6.19 | 1.55 |
+| Zeelich main street | 7.3 | 15 % | 4.86 | 0.22 |
+| Zeelich council house | 7.7 | 15 % | 5.31 | 0.88 |
+
+Census: the colliders and people within 12 m of the point 7 m ahead of him.
+
+What this says, and what the pictures show:
+1. **Not the furniture count.** Zeelich has as many lamps, benches and planters per area as the Citadel square, or
+   more. They stand in one regular line along the street.
+2. **The ground carries most of the gap: about half the fine detail and half the edges.**
+   - The Citadel's cobbles and flags have dark joints and painted relief, and its ground changes from cobble to grass,
+     dirt, beds and kerbs.
+   - Zeelich's street is one pale lilac flag edge to edge (a joint barely darker than the flag).
+   - Its houses stand on bare granite with nothing between kerb and wall.
+   - Zeelich's own textures (`ctex` in zeelich.js) never got DEPTH-LOOK's painted relief.
+3. **Empty lots and a flat skyline.**
+   - East of the plaza the street runs between granite on both sides: one house (the watch house) north and the depot
+     fence south.
+   - Every house wall is 3.6–4.3 m. Nothing in view stands taller than the council house's cap except the mills.
+4. **People.** In the frames at the dock, the gate, the main street and the council house there are fewer people than
+   on the Citadel square (2.43 per 100 m²). The plaza reaches 1.55.
+5. **Facades: not the gap** (source only).
+   - Zeelich's houses already have: recessed doors with dark reveals, an alfiz and a lintel; window frames, sills and
+     flower boxes; glass-block feet; a tiled frieze, a cornice and corner piers; caps on drums.
+   - Citadel's have: quoins, eaves, gutters, shutters, chimneys.
+   - Both read as built at the Far camera.
+6. **Lighting accents.** Both towns have lamps at a similar spacing, and their glass glows (emissive). The Citadel has
+   no extra lights either.
+
+## 2. The candidate (`src/game/zeelich29.js`, a few lines in zeelich.js)
+Everything is in Zeelich's own Esmer style, LBA2's look (`props-esmer.js` with `setLook`). Every piece is an original,
+from the shared kit.
+
+**Buildings: five Esmer buildings on the empty lots.**
+- A two-storey house with a balcony east of the north mill lane.
+- A two-storey house behind the plaza (it fills the council house's right in view 5).
+- A domed tower at the street's east end (walls 5.4 m, 9.4 m to the cap).
+- A low hall past the depot's east corner.
+- A small domed house between the south mill's lane and the depot.
+
+Each has a solid collider and is registered with worldfit. The camera's shapes come from regions.js `occAuto`.
+**They have no doors**, so no door leads nowhere.
+
+**Ground.**
+- The street's flags, kerbs and the island's granite are redrawn (`zeelich.js` `pave29Tex`, `kerb29Tex`,
+  `granite29Tex`), at the same sizes, 128–512 px:
+  - the flags' tones spread wider, some of them warmer;
+  - darker joints, a hairline crack here and there;
+  - the painted relief at 0.35–0.6.
+- Forecourts: each house's front is paved from the street to its wall in square warm flags of their own (`fore29Tex`,
+  256 px). This is visual only; his floor stays the island's bricks, with the top 0.85 cm over the slab, between the
+  gravel and the street.
+- Glazed-tile bands cross the street at each lamp pair.
+- Flower beds stand by the depot fence, the stall's back and the north house.
+
+**Life and furniture.**
+- A bin at each bench.
+- Banner poles at the gate.
+- Pennant festoons along the street's edges, from post to post. A first try hung them across the street, between the
+  camera and him; that was dropped.
+- Jars and barrels by the stall, the workshop and the hall.
+- A cage lantern (emissive, no light) at each new building's street corner.
+
+**Fitting.** Each piece is placed only where nothing stands:
+- clear of every collider, the walking lane and every door;
+- clear of the residents' stops (`walkrounds.js`) and the story's stops (`storylife.js`, `npcSpots`);
+- clear of the life places (`zlClear`), the Cistern Rise (`liftClear`) and the depot's yard.
+
+`R.z29.skipped` lists what was left out: a bin at the plaza bench (street) and one bed (crowded).
+
+**Tried and dropped** (`R.z29.cost` tallies triangles by kind):
+- Crate stacks: 0.9k triangles a crate, 11k for two.
+- A third bed.
+- A stair tower beside Mr Pelleck's house: his minaret already stands there.
+- A lantern line over the plaza: it crossed the council house's front.
+
+## 3. Cost: `renderer.info` at the five spots, switch off → on
+These are one frame's counts, all passes.
+
+| spot | draw calls | triangles |
+|---|---|---|
+| dock | 306 → 316 (+3.3 %) | 519 688 → 567 907 (+9.3 %) |
+| gate | 116 → 120 (+3.4 %) | 232 657 → 257 767 (+10.8 %) |
+| plaza | 194 → 201 (+3.6 %) | 333 599 → 379 226 (+13.7 %) |
+| main street | 164 → 174 (+6.1 %) | 419 128 → 472 450 (+12.7 %) |
+| council house | 126 → 128 (+1.6 %) | 209 969 → 231 128 (+10.1 %) |
+
+**Every spot is within the +15 % budget.**
+
+**What the candidate adds:** about 51k triangles island-wide.
+
+| kind | triangles |
+|---|---|
+| buildings | 32.7k |
+| beds | 6.3k |
+| cage lanterns | 3.5k |
+| bins | 2.8k |
+| festoons | 1.6k |
+| forecourts | 1.4k |
+| barrels | 1.2k |
+| tile bands | 0.8k |
+| jars | 1.0k |
+| banners | 0.5k |
+
+- Zeelich's Batch is one mesh per material island-wide, so most of the added triangles are drawn wherever their
+  material is in view. That is why the plaza pays for the east end.
+- Draws stay low: the pieces join the island's draw batches. 21 materials are used, most of them already the island's
+  or the kit's.
+
+**Textures.** Five new canvas textures:
+- 512 px: the granite;
+- 256 px: the street flags and the forecourt flags;
+- 128 px: the kerb and the band tiles.
+
+Three of them replace their originals when the switch is on. `renderer.info.memory.textures` was the same at every spot
+(509–517). No texture is larger than 512 px.
+
+**Not added:** no light, no shader, nothing per frame.
+
+**Not measured:** build time and memory, on a real machine.
+
+## 4. Results after (the same spots and settings)
+
+| | fine detail before → after | edges before → after | furniture /100 m² before → after |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| dock | 7.2 → 8.0 | 12 → 14 % | 7.52 → 7.96 |
+| gate | 7.6 → 12.1 | 14 → 25 % | 7.52 → 7.96 |
+| plaza | 8.3 → 13.7 | 15 → 28 % | 6.19 → 7.07 |
+| main street | 7.3 → 12.6 | 15 → 27 % | 4.86 → 5.97 |
+| council house | 7.7 → 12.1 | 15 → 24 % | 5.31 → 5.53 |
+| *Citadel square / Bug Street* | *14.6 / 13.2* | *32 / 28 %* | *5.75 / 2.65* |
+
+**Heights in view:**
+- before: walls 3.6–4.3 m (the mills apart);
+- after: the new buildings' walls reach 6.4 m, and the tower 9.4 m to its cap. They show in the main-street and
+  council-house frames.
+
+**Sheet:** `captures/zeelich-29/sheet.png` (1296×2392): five rows of before | after, then a Citadel reference row.
+
+## 5. Tests (once each, SERVE=1)
+**First pass**, with `QUERY="zeelich29=new&fortstairs=calm"`:
+- `walkers` PASS (37/0); `residents` PASS (182/0).
+- `worldfit` FAIL, 1 visual. #29's tile bands ran under the street's kerb stones 2.5 mm apart: six coplanar overlaps
+  of 0.18–0.25 m². Fixed: the bands are 5.4 m long and lie between the kerbs.
+- `zeelich-doors` 21/3. The three fail the same with both switches off. That A/B ran on this worktree's tree, not on
+  the base; the few edits that are not behind a switch only wrap materials, a no-op when off (source only). The
+  three:
+  - the terminal's door leads out 7.84 m from it, in chapters 3 and 5;
+  - Lissa's and Wenna's lines are not caught (`tl` empty).
+
+**The final tree** (both on by default, no query):
+- `walkers` PASS (37/0). It booted on `27928197`, just before the last commit, which only puts the east stall in a
+  batch of its own.
+- `worldfit` PASS (every check).
+- `zeelich-doors` 21/3: the same three pre-existing failures as above.
+
+## 6. Open: visual gaps toward the rubric (for the user)
+- **People.** Neither pass adds residents. A resident is a cast member with a name and lines (English and Hebrew), and
+  `tests/walkers.mjs` pins the cast count (47 in all, 35 waiting), so adding one is a change of its own. The life the
+  second pass adds is two gull flocks (6 birds). The street stays at 0.2–1.6 people per 100 m², against the Citadel
+  square's 2.4.
+- **Doorless houses.** The five new buildings have no door on any side. Doors that open would need rooms; doors kept
+  shut would need their lines and the Hebrew for them.
+- **The dock view barely changes** (detail 7.2 → 8.0). It sees the gate wall and the pier. A landmark seen over the
+  gate from the ferry was tried and dropped (§2).
+- **The paving's relief.** At the Far camera the plaza frame comes close to the Citadel's (13.7 against 14.6). If the
+  user finds it busy, the paint weights in `zeelich.js` `pave29Tex` (0.4) and `granite29Tex` (0.5) are the knobs.
+- **Budget headroom.** The final default adds 8–14 % triangles, against a limit of 15 %. Anything more needs geometry
+  taken out first; §7 lists what was taken out and what was dropped.
+- **Not checked on a real GPU.** One look on the GTX 1050 or UHD 620 with F9, at these five spots, would confirm the
+  cost.
+
+## 7. The second pass (the user's request of 27.11, now the default)
+Everything is again in the Esmer style, from the shared kit or painted here. There are no words on any sign. Every
+piece goes through the same fitting as §2.
+
+**Shop fronts and signs.**
+- Blade signs on brass brackets: seven of them.
+  - On three old houses, beside the door: Mr Pelleck's, the south-west house, Baldino's workshop.
+  - On the four new buildings' street corners.
+  - Each carries a painted emblem: a loaf, a jar, a cog, a flower, a cup or a fish. They come from one 256×172 atlas,
+    `sign29Tex`.
+- Striped awnings, with brass struts, over the new buildings' street-side ground windows.
+- Two notice boards with pinned papers and no words (`notice29Tex`, 128 px): at the plaza's west mouth and by the gate.
+
+**A market stall with goods.**
+- The kit's fruit stall, on the east street's north side.
+- It is a batch of its own: inside the island's per-material meshes it made the plaza frame draw 32k more triangles.
+- Its canopy is a camera volume, as the plaza stall's is (`roomOcc`, the API only).
+- A cloth stall across from the workshop was tried and dropped for the budget.
+
+**Landmarks and cloth.**
+- Two 7.2 m flag masts at the street's east end, either side of the platform's gate, in view down the main street with
+  the domed tower.
+- A laundry line with hanging cloth before the south house.
+
+**Life.** Two small gull flocks (`gulls.js`, 3 birds each) perch on the plaza's lamps, the fountain's rim, the stall's
+canopy and the east street's new roofs and lamps. They take off when he comes close. Their cost:
+- 2 instanced draws a flock;
+- no shadow;
+- simulated only while he is on Zeelich.
+
+**Geometry taken out to pay for it.** Under the default, the street's 18 lamps use 6-sided turnings and slimmer rings.
+That is about half of their 0.9k triangles a lamp, and they read the same at the Far camera.
+
+**`renderer.info` at the five spots, the original → the final default** (one frame, all passes):
+
+| spot | draw calls | triangles |
+|---|---|---|
+| dock | 306 → 324 (+5.9 %) | 519 688 → 571 369 (+9.9 %) |
+| gate | 116 → 120 (+3.4 %) | 232 657 → 252 185 (+8.4 %) |
+| plaza | 194 → 205 (+5.7 %) | 333 599 → 376 671 (+12.9 %) |
+| main street | 164 → 183 (+11.6 %) | 419 128 → 476 724 (+13.7 %) |
+| council house | 126 → 133 (+5.6 %) | 209 969 → 231 415 (+10.2 %) |
+
+**Every spot is within +15 %.**
+
+What the numbers above leave out:
+- **Added geometry:** 61k triangles in all, island-wide (`R.z29.cost`). The largest parts:
+  - buildings 32.7k;
+  - beds 6.3k;
+  - the stall 5.9k;
+  - cage lanterns 3.5k;
+  - bins 2.8k;
+  - signs 1.5k.
+- **Materials:** 30 in use.
+- **Textures:** `renderer.info.memory.textures` rose by 5–6 at each spot. All are canvas textures of 512 px or less.
+
+**Frames** (fine detail, before → after): dock 7.2 → 8.0, gate 7.6 → 12.2, plaza 8.3 → 13.7, main street 7.3 → 12.7,
+council house 7.7 → 12.3. The Citadel square is 14.6.
+
+**Furniture per 100 m²:** gate 7.5 → 8.2, plaza 6.2 → 7.1, main street 4.9 → 6.4, council house 5.3 → 5.8.
+
+**Sheet:** `captures/zeelich-29/sheet-2.png` (1296×2392). Before is the original street, after is the final default;
+the same five spots, and the Citadel reference row.
+
+## For the user
+It is the default (your pick). `?zeelich29=old` shows the street as it was, for comparison.
+
+Still open:
+- residents with routines on the new east street (§6: cast, lines, Hebrew, the walkers suite's count);
+- doors for the new buildings;
+- a real-GPU look.
