+// #29 (OPEN-TASKS.he.md, the user: "Zeelich looks simpler than the Citadel"): the candidate `?zeelich29=new`, picked by
+// the user 27.11 and ON by default since. `?zeelich29=old` turns it off: then nothing here runs (zeelich.js calls
+// buildZeelich29 only under Z29.on, and z29Clear answers false) and the island is exactly as before.
+//
+// Measured against the Citadel from the play camera (docs/lba-maturity/ZEELICH-29.md): Zeelich's street is one row of
+// five low houses (3.6–4.3 m walls) with long empty stretches east of the plaza and by the gate, its furniture only
+// lamps, benches and planters in a regular line, its paving one flat colour edge to edge, nothing in the air over the
+// street, and no building taller than the council house's cap in view. What this adds, in Zeelich's own Esmer language
+// (props-esmer.js, LBA2's look: setLook), all original pieces from the shared kit:
+//   - six Esmer buildings on the empty lots, so the street reads as a town and its skyline steps: a two-storey house
+//     with a balcony east of the north mill lane, another behind the plaza, a domed tower at the east end (the landmark
+//     down the street from the plaza), a low hall by the depot's east corner, and a small domed house between the south
+//     mill's lane and the depot. (A slim stair tower beside Mr Pelleck's house was planned for the view from the gate:
+//     his house's minaret already stands there.) They have no doors at all (door: false: no door that leads nowhere; a gap listed for the user); each
+//     registered with worldfit; solid colliders; the camera's own tall-solid shapes (regions.js occAuto);
+//   - pennant festoons along the street's edges, lamp post to lamp post;
+//   - forecourts: each house's front paved from the street to its wall in square flags of their own (zeelich.js fore29Tex);
+//   - the street's flags, kerbs and the island's granite with more contrast and the painted relief (zeelich.js *29Tex);
+//   - on the ground: glazed-tile bands across the street at each lamp pair (the paving's rhythm), flower beds before
+//     the depot's fence and the new houses;
+//   - street life: a bin at each bench, goods by the new houses and the stall (crates, jars, barrels), banner poles at
+//     the gate, a cage lantern at each new house's street corner.
+// Every piece is fitted where nothing stands (fit below): clear of every collider built before it, the street's
+// walking lane, every door, the story's and the residents' stops (walkrounds.js, storylife.js, zeelich.js npcSpots), the
+// street's life places (zeelife.js zlClear), the Cistern Rise (zlift.js liftClear), the depot's yard (its fence and the
+// beats inside it: DEPOT below); a piece that does not fit is left out (R.z29.skipped lists it). Colliders for everything he can
+// walk into (low pieces see-through for the camera, the buildings solid). Static parts go into the island's Batch (one
+// mesh per material, as the rest of the street); the props' materials are the shared kit's (kit.js/props-esmer.js).
+import * as THREE from 'three';
+import { Place, esmerBuilding, setLook, capM, bin, barrel, jars, flowerBed, bannerPole, cageLamp, hangingLine, stall, flagPole, laundry, EM, cm, tileTex } from './props-esmer.js';
